1
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,233
Welcome, Voyager.

2
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:21,933
If this tape has reached you, you were noticed.

3
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,533
The Multiverse Collective existed for many years for only one purpose:

4
00:00:27,867 --> 00:00:33,300
to find the worlds beside this one — and to watch them.

5
00:00:33,667 --> 00:00:36,533
Not imagine them. Watch them.

6
00:00:36,967 --> 00:00:40,400
So from today, you are part of the work.

7
00:00:43,133 --> 00:00:46,400
This is the Multiverse Console.

8
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,700
It will live in your home.

9
00:00:48,733 --> 00:00:51,767
This one is the frequency dial.

10
00:00:51,767 --> 00:00:57,067
Every frequency is a parallel world that exists.

11
00:00:57,067 --> 00:01:00,667
Close to the right number, you will see shapes.

12
00:01:00,767 --> 00:01:04,467
On it, you may see a certain place.

13
00:01:08,167 --> 00:01:10,967
And this one — the band dial.

14
00:01:11,133 --> 00:01:15,167
It chooses where, in that world, it watches from.

15
00:01:18,433 --> 00:01:21,300
And this — the quantum energy button.

16
00:01:21,367 --> 00:01:22,900
Hold it. Wait.

17
00:01:23,567 --> 00:01:26,700
What will happen next depends on the world.

18
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,500
A handler has been assigned to you.

19
00:01:32,567 --> 00:01:34,267
You will be listening to him —

20
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,000
I'm Will.

21
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:40,900
Before the Collective, I made games at NetEase and hardware at ByteDance.

22
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:45,967
A game with a million daily players. A device that sold two million units.

23
00:01:46,067 --> 00:01:47,567
But I thought that was boring.

24
00:01:47,567 --> 00:01:52,567
Only after I joined the Collective did I find this machine — a special device.

25
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,667
I have to find more people to work with me, together, to find different worlds.

26
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:02,333
Rule one.

27
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:05,400
Their time runs with ours.

28
00:02:05,733 --> 00:02:08,667
What you miss does not come back.

29
00:02:08,733 --> 00:02:09,533
Rule two.

30
00:02:09,633 --> 00:02:12,133
You will never see all of it.

31
00:02:12,167 --> 00:02:17,567
Other Voyagers who hold these devices will see what you cannot.

32
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:18,767
Write down everything.

33
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:23,467
Write down every frequency you have found in the device.

34
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:24,400
Rule four.

35
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:26,933
If the light turns red —

36
00:02:27,533 --> 00:02:32,700
— it means they may be looking back at our world.

37
00:02:33,033 --> 00:02:34,167
End of orientation.

38
00:02:34,567 --> 00:02:35,967
Stay on the frequency.
